WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.802
-Our next guest is an
Emmy-nominated comedian

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:05.638
and actress who stars in the hit
series "Abbott Elementary."

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:08.641
The winter finale airs
this Wednesday on ABC,

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:10.743
with new episodes
returning January 4th.

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:11.878
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:13.346
-It's time
for the gift exchange.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.848
Let's find out who's been
naughty and who's been nice.

00:00:15.848 --> 00:00:18.517
And remember,
I only reward the naughty.

00:00:18.517 --> 00:00:21.554
Everyone who picked a name
out of Mr. Johnson's ice skate

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:23.289
last week,
please gather 'round.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:24.924
-Dorothy Hamill and I
used to be a thing.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:27.059
This is all I have left of her.

00:00:27.059 --> 00:00:30.129
-Okay, I hope you guys
all stuck to the $25 minimum.

00:00:30.129 --> 00:00:32.031
-Um, I thought
that was a maximum.

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:33.866
-Stop limiting yourself.
Thinking small is

00:00:33.866 --> 00:00:36.302
what's got you in a dead-end job
in a poorly run school.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:38.004
-Can't argue with that.

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:40.740
-Please welcome back to the show
our friend Janelle James!

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.808
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.808 --> 00:00:45.845
[ Mid-tempo music plays ]

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:51.350
♪♪

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:56.890
♪♪

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.025
Now, Janelle,
I'm so happy you're here.

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:02.428
You are one of our favorite
kinds of returning guests,

00:01:02.428 --> 00:01:06.066
because you were first here
in 2019 as a stand-up.

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:07.400
-Yes!
-You did five minutes with us.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.068
-I did.
-I was not lucky enough

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:11.003
to have you even sitting
here next to me.

00:01:11.003 --> 00:01:13.139
-Oh, my God.
I was so nervous there, too.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.074
I'm looking at the picture.
That's my nervous hand

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:16.576
that's up like that.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:18.444
And now people yell at me
in Target,

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:20.480
so this is nothing.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:23.516
-I mean, we're so happy with
how everything's going for you.

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:27.186
Are you overwhelmed by it, or
does this make perfect sense?

00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:29.455
-Uh, both.
-Yeah, I think that's right.

00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:30.789
-Yeah.
-I think that's right.

00:01:30.789 --> 00:01:32.758
-I was working towards it, but
it's still like, "Aah!

00:01:32.758 --> 00:01:34.293
What's happening?"
So, yeah.

00:01:34.293 --> 00:01:36.595
No, but it's all been great.
It's so good to be, like,

00:01:36.595 --> 00:01:39.531
on something that seems to make
so many people so happy.

00:01:39.531 --> 00:01:41.968
-Yeah, and it seems like
a show for so many people,

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.702
which is so nice
in this day and age.

00:01:43.702 --> 00:01:46.406
You were at the Emmys.
The show was

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:48.074
very well represented
at the Emmys,

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:49.875
which was wonderful.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:49.875 --> 00:01:52.745
Was it your --
Was it your first Emmys?

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:55.614
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:01:55.614 --> 00:01:57.750
I mean, I think I had
a men's undershirt on in this.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.485
Like, I've never
been to the Emmys.

00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:01.654
I don't even know whose clothes
I have on right now.

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:03.990
But, yes,
my first time at the Emmys.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:07.826
My first time being nominated.
And, yeah, it was wild.

00:02:07.826 --> 00:02:10.863
-Did you -- You know,
sometimes the logistics

00:02:10.863 --> 00:02:14.433
of the Emmys are an obstacle
course in their own right.

00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:16.235
Did you make it in time?

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:17.904
-He know I was late.
That's why he brought that up.

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:19.806
[ Laughter ]
He knew I was late.

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:23.376
Yes. No,
I didn't make it in time, Seth.

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:25.411
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:26.912
-I'm just curious.
I mean, I guess

00:02:26.912 --> 00:02:29.047
if I could ask one question
out of the blue...

00:02:29.047 --> 00:02:32.185
-I was late to my first Emmys.
I mean, it's a story now.

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:34.654
So, it's a story
that I get to tell.

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:36.255
But I wasn't the only one,
so that's all that matters.

00:02:36.255 --> 00:02:38.657
-Yeah. It's not --
They make it very hard

00:02:38.657 --> 00:02:39.959
to be on time at the Emmys.
-Yeah.

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:41.527
-I'm saying that genuinely.
But what about you --

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:43.128
Do you get to go to Hollywood
fancy parties now?

00:02:43.128 --> 00:02:45.764
How is that treating you?
-I mean, I do get to go to --

00:02:45.764 --> 00:02:48.267
I don't go to many,
and then when I do,

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:50.103
it's just a disaster
because I'm not --

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:52.538
I guess I'm not trained
to do the thing.

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:54.640
-That looks pretty good.
I feel like -- Do that.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:57.476
Yeah, oh, I think,
don't sell yourself short.

00:02:57.476 --> 00:02:59.578
I've seen a lot of high-powered
agents do exactly that.

00:02:59.578 --> 00:03:01.747
-I practice in the mirror

00:03:01.747 --> 00:03:04.716
ever since I embarrassed myself.
I went to the "GQ" party.

00:03:04.716 --> 00:03:05.951
Were you there?
-No, I was not

00:03:05.951 --> 00:03:08.621
at the "GQ" party, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:11.691
-I was. I was there.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:16.895
I went to the "GQ" party,
and I saw Travis Barker.

00:03:16.895 --> 00:03:19.832
-Uh-huh.
-The Blink-182 guy.

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:23.702
The reason I know who he is, is,
truly when I was getting ready,

00:03:23.702 --> 00:03:25.938
earlier that day,
for the party,

00:03:25.938 --> 00:03:28.708
I was watching a video of him
showing his home

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:30.743
with one of those Kardashians.
-Yeah.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:33.446
-Right?
-He's famously with one of them.

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.581
-One of them.
Still don't know which one.

00:03:35.581 --> 00:03:37.149
And --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.149 --> 00:03:40.486
But the home was lovely, and
he seemed like such a nice guy.

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:42.722
Every piece in his house
had a meaning,

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:45.157
and it wasn't ostentatious.
It was really nice.

00:03:45.157 --> 00:03:48.094
And I saw him at the party.
Yeah, I'm drunk. I was nervous.

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:50.963
But I saw him at the party,
and he walked by,

00:03:50.963 --> 00:03:52.231
and I said, "Oh, my God,

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:53.733
I was just looking
in your house."

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:56.769
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:59.639
[ Applause ]

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:01.073
And that's --
That's why I stay home.

00:04:01.073 --> 00:04:03.209
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:05.311
How does a fella respond

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.645
when you say you were
just looking at his house?

00:04:06.645 --> 00:04:09.449
-So, the Kardashian said,
"Okay," like that.

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:11.651
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:14.086
They looked horrified.
He looked horrified.

00:04:14.086 --> 00:04:15.888
-Yeah.
-And she said, "Okay."

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:17.790
And then they, like, walked off.
-Still hasn't really

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.191
narrowed it down for me
which one it is.

00:04:19.191 --> 00:04:21.761
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:23.896
You -- One of the things --

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:26.398
obviously, we first met you here
as a stand-up.

00:04:26.398 --> 00:04:30.336
That's this real solo art form
where you get to tell the story

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:32.371
entirely by yourself.
You know, you're just out there

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:34.840
totally by yourself.
-And I am myself.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:36.141
-You get to be yourself,
exactly.

00:04:36.141 --> 00:04:37.376
You get to choose what you say.

00:04:37.376 --> 00:04:39.946
Obviously, this role
seems to be a perfect fit,

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:41.980
but it's also
a wonderful ensemble.

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:43.816
How have you found that shift
from, you know,

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:46.052
sort of being on your own to
being in a world full of --

00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:49.222
-I work less.
-Yeah, you do. You do work less.

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:51.790
-When you're an ensemble,
it's not only about you.

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:54.727
So I get some time off,
where the story

00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:57.730
focuses on other people
and the --

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.732
I just learned this thing
with the actors,

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:02.968
where actors say, "You're only
as good as your scene partner."

00:05:02.968 --> 00:05:05.605
And so it's really good actors
on this show,

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:09.208
and it makes me step up
and have my [Bleep] together.

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:11.710
-And you guys all really do feel
like you've known each other.

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:13.178
-Truly.
-The show only works

00:05:13.178 --> 00:05:15.147
if you only believe you've known
each other for a long time,

00:05:15.147 --> 00:05:17.316
working together long time,
and it's just so natural.

00:05:17.316 --> 00:05:19.752
-I think partly it's because
we're all cool people,

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:23.322
but also we started this show,
like, right out of quarantine.

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:26.058
We couldn't go nowhere.
Couldn't go anywhere

00:05:26.058 --> 00:05:28.027
but work and hang out
with each other, you know.

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:30.229
We were the only safe people
that we knew at the time.

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:32.931
So it really made us closer
in a faster way,

00:05:32.931 --> 00:05:35.667
having to do -- you know,
having to do it at that time.

00:05:35.667 --> 00:05:37.269
-I've been lucky to talk
to some other cast members

00:05:37.269 --> 00:05:38.371
of the show.
They were saying

00:05:38.371 --> 00:05:39.672
the technical aspect
of the show,

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:41.774
the way you shoot, because
it's documentary style,

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:44.076
there's a real choreography
to every scene.

00:05:44.076 --> 00:05:45.711
Do you feel like you're
getting better at that,

00:05:45.711 --> 00:05:47.513
being able to know
the camera's coming?

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:49.281
-I mean, I thought I was good
from the beginning, so, um...

00:05:49.281 --> 00:05:52.051
-Yeah, yeah.
I think everybody agrees.

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:55.321
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:56.889
-I'm not --
-I guess my question is,

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:59.758
do you feel like your castmates
are catching up to your --

00:05:59.758 --> 00:06:02.394
-To me?
Tyler got some work to do.

00:06:02.394 --> 00:06:04.597
But, uh, yeah.

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:06.465
I feel like, because
I didn't know anything...

00:06:06.465 --> 00:06:08.067
-Yeah.
-...I'm just doing it.

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:10.102
Until somebody
tells me otherwise,

00:06:10.102 --> 00:06:11.637
I'm just gonna
keep doing what I'm doing.

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:13.572
-Well, I think
everybody here agrees

00:06:13.572 --> 00:06:15.140
that that's
the best plan forward.

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:16.375
So nice to see you again.
-Yes!

00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:17.910
-Thank you for being here.
-Thank you so much.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.746
-You guys, that's Janelle James.

00:06:19.746 --> 00:06:22.048
The winter finale
of "Abbott Elementary"

00:06:22.048 --> 00:06:23.649
airs this Wednesday on ABC,

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:25.451
with new episodes returning
January 4th.

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:27.220
We'll be right back
with an incredible performance

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:28.721
of "Funny Girl."

